SILK goldens, generated from libopus 1.6.1 in the default configuration
(plain ./configure: no DRED, deep PLC or OSCE; FLOAT_APPROX and
ENABLE_RES24 on), built as the scalar reference (--disable-intrinsics
--disable-rtcd --disable-asm, CFLAGS=-ffp-contract=off). The C drivers
link .libs/libopus.a of that tree and compile with -include config.h,
so that the control structures have its layout; they refuse to build
against a tree with ENABLE_DEEP_PLC, ENABLE_OSCE or ENABLE_DRED.

The drivers and the generator script are in tools/oracle/silk/
(dec.c: decoder, enc.c and unit.c: encoder). Regenerate and compare
with the committed files (see tools/oracle/README.md for the
environment):

  tools/oracle/silk/gen.sh       # compare
  tools/oracle/silk/gen.sh -w    # also copy into this directory

SILK decoder goldens
--------------------

The decoder driver does what runSILK in harness_test.go does: it splits
an Opus stream into frames (opus_packet_parse), skips CELT-only frames
(and calls silk_ResetDecoder on the next SILK frame), and decodes the
SILK part of every SILK-only and hybrid frame with silk_Decode. Loss
simulation: an LCG (x = x*1103515245 + 12345, lost when
(x>>16) % 100 < 15) marks frames lost; loss mode 1 conceals them
(lostFlag 1), loss mode 2 decodes the LBRR data of the next frame
(lostFlag 2). Frames of 0 or 1 bytes (DTX) are concealed. Each
silk_Decode call prints

	frame lostFlag ret nSamplesOut finalRange prevPitchLag fnv1a64(float samples)

The golden is the first 32 hex digits of the SHA-256 of all lines and
the number of lines. Set SILK_DUMP_DIR when running TestVectors or
TestMix to write the Go lines for diffing against the driver output
($OPUS_WORK/silk/c/dec, $OPUS_WORK/silk/c/mix).

vectors_golden.txt  RFC 8251 test vectors 02-06, 08-10, 12 (the ones with
                    SILK or hybrid frames) at API rates 8/12/16/24/48 kHz,
                    1 and 2 API channels, loss modes 0/1/2. Needs
                    OPUS_TESTVECTORS.
silk_mix.bit        40 KB stream in the test vector format, made by
                    concatenating short opus_demo -e voip encodings (NB 10
                    ms, MB 20 ms stereo, WB 40/60 ms, SWB hybrid, MB/NB
                    40/60 ms, with -inbandfec and -dtx) of test vector
                    audio. It covers LBRR, DTX/CNG and mode switches.
mix_golden.txt      Goldens for silk_mix.bit, same configurations.
mix_samples_16k_mono_plc.raw
                    First 4096 output samples (int16 LE) of silk_mix.bit
                    at 16 kHz mono with loss mode 1.

SILK encoder goldens
--------------------

The encoder driver (enc.c) reads the PCM and the per-packet control
script that TestWriteEncGoldenInputs writes (OPUS_GOLDEN_INPUTS=dir;
add OPUS_TESTVECTORS for the vector scenarios). For each packet it fills
silk_EncControlStruct from the script, calls silk_Encode on a fresh
ec_enc over a maxBytes buffer (maxBits = 8 * maxBytes), calls
ec_enc_done, and decodes the packet with silk_Decode (lostFlag 1 for
empty packets). It prints, per packet,

	idx prefill ret nBytes ec_tell finalRange switchReady internalSampleRate
	inWBmodeWithoutVariableLP stereoWidth_Q14 signalType offset
	allowBandwidthSwitch maxBits fnv1a64(buffer)

and a final line "dec fnv1a64(decoded int16) nSamples". The golden is
the line count and the first 32 hex digits of the SHA-256 of all
lines ("s" lines), plus the first lines of each scenario ("l" lines).
Set SILK_ENC_DUMP to write the Go lines ($OPUS_WORK/silk/c/enc has the
C lines).

enc_golden.txt          Synthetic input (enc_synth_test.go): fixed
                        configurations over API rates 8-48 kHz, 1/2
                        channels, 10-60 ms, complexity 0-10, FEC, DTX,
                        CBR; a 22 s stream; and 24 streams with randomly
                        varying controls (bitrate, complexity, frame
                        size, FEC/loss, DTX, CBR, maxBits, internal rate
                        limits, opusCanSwitch, stereo/mono with toMono,
                        reducedDependency, prefill 1/2, VAD activity).
enc_vectors_golden.txt  The decoded RFC 8251 test vectors
                        (testvectorNN.dec) through four configurations
                        each. Needs OPUS_TESTVECTORS.
enc_unit_golden.txt     Hashes of silk_A2NLSF, silk_LPC_inverse_pred_gain_FLP,
                        silk_residual_energy_covar_FLP, silk_schur_FLP and
                        silk_autocorrelation_FLP on random inputs (unit.c).

The encoder packets are the same in the default and the DNN-enabled
libopus builds; only the final "dec" line (the decoder round trip, which
conceals empty packets) differs in some scenarios.
